0,Samaritan Hebrew - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samaritan_Hebrew,"Today, the spoken vernacular among Samaritans is evenly split between Modern Hebrew and Samaritan Arabic, depending on whether they reside in Holon or Kiryat Luza. The early history of Samaritan Hebrew is poorly documented, though it cannot be easily associated with early Israelian Hebrew.",Samaritan Hebrew,Afro-Asiatic
